ZUGFeRD 1.0
-----------

The archive io/github/nalukit/paniolo/rules/facturx/zugferd-1.0-2014-06-25.zip
holds the XSD schemas and the Schematron of ZUGFeRD 1.0 (FeRD, 2014-06-25),
which FeRD no longer publishes. They are taken unmodified from the Mustang
project (https://github.com/ZUGFeRD/mustangproject, Apache License 2.0),
as last changed there in commit 42795b17 (2021-05-09):

  schema/ZUGFeRD1p0*.xsd          validator/src/main/resources/schema/ZF_10/
  schematron/ZUGFeRD_1p0.sch      validator/src/main/resources/ZUGFeRD_1p0.sch
  schematron/ZUGFeRD_1p0.xslt     validator/src/main/resources/xslt/ZUGFeRD_1p0.xslt
                                  (the Schematron compiled to XSLT by the
                                  Mustang project)

SHA256SUMS in the archive lists the checksum of each file. The Schematron
carries the original terms of use of FeRD for the ZUGFeRD data format 1.0
(free licence for the use and further development of the data format in
software); FeRD states that the Apache License 2.0 applies to the technical
artifacts (schemas and Schematron) of the ZUGFeRD standard (see above).
Mustangproject, Copyright 2014 Jochen Staerk, Apache License 2.0.

EXTENDED-CTC-FR (France)
------------------------

The archive io/github/nalukit/paniolo/rules/facturx/<france.archive>.zip
(exact version and SHA-256 in facturx-rules.properties) holds the CII rules
of the French profile EXTENDED-CTC-FR and the French rules BR-FR (flux 2)
of the e-invoicing reform (XP Z12-012), published by FNFE-MPE (Forum
National de la Facture Electronique et des Marches Publics Electroniques):

  France_RFE, release tag v1.4.0.04 (2026-09-04)
  https://github.com/fnfempe/France_RFE/releases/tag/v1.4.0.04

It contains, unmodified and with their original paths, the files of the
folder FNFE_RFE_INVOICE/CII/EXTENDED-CTC-FR (Schematron and compiled XSLT),
the LICENSE of the repository, and SHA256SUMS with the checksum of each
file.

  Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE in the archive and
  META-INF/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt)

Order-X 1.0
-----------

The archive io/github/nalukit/paniolo/rules/facturx/order-x-1.0-2021-04-13.zip
holds the technical artifacts of Order-X 1.0 (English release of
2021-04-13), published by AWV e.V. (FeRD) and FNFE-MPE: for the profiles
Basic, Comfort and Extended the XSD schemas and the Schematron of the
folder 04-XSD-UML-SCHEMATRON, unmodified and with their original paths,
and the terms of use of the release (Nutzungsrechte.txt, Disclaimer.txt):

  "The Apache 2.0 license terms apply to the use of the Order-X technical
  artifacts."

The files <level>/Schematron/SCRDMCCBDACIOMessageStructure_100pD20B_<LEVEL>.xslt
are not part of the release: they are the Schematron of the release
compiled to XSLT with SVRL output by Paniolo (scripts/package-orderx-rules.sh,
ISO Schematron skeleton, MIT License, and Saxon-HE). SHA256SUMS in the
archive marks each file as official or compiled. Order-X is based on the
UN/CEFACT Supply Chain Reference Data Model and the Cross Industry Order;
the terms of use of UNECE apply accordingly.

The generated XSLT files include utility templates from the ISO Schematron
skeleton by Rick Jelliffe and Academia Sinica Computing Centre, Taiwan:
  https://github.com/Schematron/schematron/tree/master/trunk/schematron/code
Their MIT license and copyright notices are retained in
META-INF/licenses/MIT-ISO-Schematron.txt and in
licenses/MIT-ISO-Schematron.txt inside the Order-X archive.
